\f0\fs22 \cf0 TextMouth carries the code of these projects, and follows the code of three decoders. The licence of each is in the app, in its Licenses folder.\
\

\f1\b FFmpeg
\f0\b0 \
This software uses libraries from the FFmpeg project under the LGPLv2.1. TextMouth converts Windows Media, Matroska and WebM, AVI, Flash video, RealMedia, Musepack, and Speex with FFmpeg 9.0.2 and five upstream patches (each named by its commit in FFmpeg's notice, in the app's Licenses folder), in a helper program of its own. Licence: the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.\
\

\f1\b LAME
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth writes MP3 with the LAME encoder, version 3.100. Licence: the GNU Library General Public License, version 2.\
\

\f1\b liblouis
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth translates braille with liblouis, version 3.39.0, and its braille tables, in a helper program of its own. Licence: the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.\
\

\f1\b SwiftSoup
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth reads HTML and XML with SwiftSoup, version 2.13.9. Licence: the MIT License.\
\

\f1\b ZIPFoundation
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth reads and writes ZIP archives with ZIPFoundation, version 0.9.20. Licence: the MIT License.\
\

\f1\b swift-cmark
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth reads Markdown with swift-cmark, version 0.9.0, the cmark-gfm parser. Licence: the BSD 2-Clause License, with the licences of the parts it includes.\
\

\f1\b foliate-js
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth's MOBI reader follows the mobi.js of foliate-js. Licence: the MIT License.\
\

\f1\b The TTA, WavPack, and Monkey's Audio decoders
\f0\b0 \
TextMouth's own readers of True Audio, WavPack, and Monkey's Audio files follow the decoders of the TTA Hardware Players Library 1.2, libwavpack 5.9.0, and the Monkey's Audio SDK 13.47. Licence: the BSD 3-Clause License, as each decoder's notice says.}
